*Infinite [[Sir Rel]]s spawn after 166.67 seconds<sup>5,000f</sup>, delay 66.67~70 seconds<sup>2,000f~2,100f</sup>.

==Strategy==
It is recommended to rush the stage using a combination of [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]], [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:N2]], and [[Cossack Cat (Rare Cat)|Royal Guard]]/[[Food Stall Cat (Rare Cat)|Cafeteria Cat]]. [[Battle Items#Rich Cat|Rich Cat]] makes this strategy more consistent but isn't necessary.

*Z-Kill the Zroco and stall the opening Kang Roos for a few seconds, then kill them with any [[:Category:Cats with Money Up ability|Double Bounty unit]].
*Once Jumbo Jones spawns, lure him very close to your base and start chaining him with with a combination of the aforementioned units, along with [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cats]] to clear the way of peons. Thanks to his high knockback count and drawn-out foreswing animation, it is nigh impossible for him to finish his attack cycle before staggering repeatedly.
**If it looks as though Jumbo Jones is going to get an attack off, use the Cat Cannon or a well-timed [[Battle Items#Sniper the Cat|Sniper the Cat]] item to reset his attack animation.
*By the time he reaches Oldhorn, he should either be at very low HP or outright dead depending on how efficiently you chained him.
**If he's knocked behind Oldhorn and decimates your stack of units, lure him back to the Cat Base and try chaining him with any fast, high DPH units like [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] and [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]].
*Once Jumbo Jones is dead, the cleanup phase is fairly tame. If your Idi:N2 is still alive after the initial chain, she should be able to clear the Oldhorn with relative ease along with Awakened Bahamut Cat. Royal Guard Cat in particular wipes the field of Oldhorn, and works phenomenally as cleanup in the event the your initial chain fails.

Lord Gravey will not be much of an issue on his own after the dust settles. Just bring any anti-Zombie unit that outranges him, e.g. [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]], and whittle him down until the victory is yours.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Sonic (Uber Rare Cat)|Sonic]]: Sonic's mobility and huge damage against Angels allows him to deal insanely high damage against Jumbo Jones. Be careful with using him, as allowing Jumbo Jones to be knocked back too much could allow him to go behind Oldhorn prematurely.
*Any Anti-Zombie which outranges Gravey can be used to make chipping him down take less than an eternity. Examples include [[Shining Amaterasu (Uber Rare Cat)|Almighty Amaterasu]] and most ubers from the [[Frontline Assault IRON LEGION (Gacha Event)|IRON LEGION]] banner.
*[[Detective Vigler (Uber Rare Cat)|Section Chief Gravicci]]: Provides a great research combo which can leave more space for other combos or usable units on top of being able to speed up clearing out the Lord Gravey.
*[[Kasa Jizo (Uber Rare Cat)|Ultra Kasa Jizo]]: Jizo's high dps when stacked can be amazing for juggling Jones. His power is amplified even more when using research combos like [[Biohazard (Combo)|Biohazard]], [[Bony Bone (Combo)|Bony Bone]], or even [[Bad Guys (Combo)|Bad Guys]] if you have [[Lasvoss (Uber Rare Cat)|Lasvoss]].

